Z||000000||ChadMan||07-12-99||07:49 AM||||The Fiero Owners Club of America National meet is in Columbus, OH, August 12-15.<p>Anybody coming?  I've been reading about you guys' Fieros for months now and I'd like to see them.  
Z||000001||87GT||07-12-99||09:45 AM||||Ive tried to join FOCOA.  I sent in a check over 4 weeks ago to join and have yet to hear anything.  Their site is all messed up too.  I cant even send an email.  I would like to go but...
Z||000002||Eric||07-12-99||02:48 PM||||Screw FOCOA!  I'm just going to go.  I don't think you have to be a member.  I live in Columbus, so it wouldn't be a big deal for me to have to turn around and go home, but maybe it would be for someone from another state.<p>I don't know if my rebuild/restoration will be done by then.  I haven't even pulled my engine out yet.  If it's not ready by next month, who cares?  I'll bring pictures if anyone wants to see it.<p>Hey, if anybody wants to go but is not sure of where to stay or eat, go to the COFE website and it will tell you everything you need to know, even directions.  Or you could ask me.
Z||000003||GREENDANO||07-12-99||04:11 PM||||Hey Eric, How about a URL?  I'm interested!!!<br>  Dan-O
Z||000004||Eric||07-12-99||05:16 PM||||Oops, sorry.  It's www.ohiofiero.com.
Z||000005||ChadMan||07-13-99||07:29 AM||||FOCOA can be frustrating.  I tried to call them 5 times to order some seat covers and register for the show by phone, but kept getting an automated answering system.  I left my name and number, but they never returned my calls, so I gave up and sent in a check.  Hope they get it...<p>FOCOA's not perfect, but as long as they hold national meets, I'll remain a member.  I think it's worth the hassle to come to the Nationals, and see everyone's cars, and hang out with people who appreciate Fieros. 
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||07-13-99||03:43 PM||||I really can't comment on FOCOA since I'm in Europe, but currently there's a discussion going on on the Fiero Mailing List. It seems that lately a lot of people are having difficulties getting anything from them. Memberships, parts, newsletters et al. Checks are being cashed, but nothing is being sent. Phonecalls are not being answered and their website doesn't exist anymore. Ordinarily I would say this is a clear cut case of bankruptcy but I hope for people's sake it's just a temporary logistics problem they're experiencing because they have just moved.<br>
Z||000007||87GT||07-13-99||04:18 PM||||I will be very pissed if that check gets cashed and I dont get anything.  
Z||000008||Gokart||07-13-99||07:25 PM||||It took 2 months and 3 phone calls (714)903-6186 for me to finally get my stuff. After finally getting it they spelled my first AND last name wrong on my membership card! I sent it back last week requesting a new one. Unless their site comes back up on a consistent basis I wouldn't do any ordering with them. At least we got 1-800-fierogt! Living on Cape Cod I think I'll have to miss the convention in Ohio!
Z||000009||batboy||07-13-99||10:52 PM||||When I joined the FOCOA, it took them a while to send me the first magazine, but I'm getting them now. Never had to phone them though.
